From 8a4d9f8e50fc74554736bed7f18d8702a04b02d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <zenithblue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:43:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] panvk/jm: the TLS/WLS pool skips the kbase CPU clear

Rationale: perf review 2026-10-26, finding D2 (quick part, second half;
the first half, command pool auto-trim on JM, is P-B's 0005). The JM
command buffer TLS pool holds only the per-half TLS and WLS buffers of
jm-v7 107 (cmd_close_batch_impl()), and kbase_kmod_bo_alloc() memset and
synced every committed page of each new one (csf-v11 041): 40.5 + 6.75 MiB
per half on the S9 (2324 B tessellator stacks over a core-ID range of 27),
92 MiB per half on the Pixel 6, so a command buffer with a tessellated
draw spent 10-30 ms of CPU on its first use of each half, and again for
every other command buffer and after every pool trim.

Shaders never read either before writing it: stack slots are written
before they are read, WLS is undefined at dispatch start
(zero-initialized workgroup memory is lowered in the shader), and pooled
BOs are already handed out again uncleared. The pool now asks for
PAN_KMOD_BO_FLAG_NO_ZERO (P-B 0003), as the CSF TLS and WLS pools do;
kbase still hands out zeroed pages except this context's own freed ones.

Knob: PANVK_KBASE_ZERO_ALL=1 (P-B's) clears these BOs again (114). Arch:
v6/v7/v9 (JM). Non-kbase kmods mask the flag (panvk_device_adjust_bo_flags()).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c
index f239d45c..f991c562 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c
@@ -669,9 +669,15 @@ panvk_create_cmdbuf(struct vk_command_pool *vk_pool, VkCommandBufferLevel level,
    panvk_pool_init(&cmdbuf->desc_pool, device, &pool->desc_bo_pool, NULL,
                    &desc_pool_props);
 
+   /* Only TLS (stacks, written before they are read) and WLS (undefined
+    * at dispatch start, zero-init is lowered in the shader) come from this
+    * pool, and pooled BOs are reused uncleared anyway: no kbase clear, as
+    * the CSF TLS does (perf review 2026-10-26 D2; up to 2 x 47 MiB of
+    * memset per command buffer on the S9). PANVK_KBASE_ZERO_ALL=1 clears
+    * them again. */
    struct panvk_pool_properties tls_pool_props = {
-      .create_flags =
-         panvk_device_adjust_bo_flags(device, PAN_KMOD_BO_FLAG_NO_MMAP),
+      .create_flags = panvk_device_adjust_bo_flags(
+         device, PAN_KMOD_BO_FLAG_NO_MMAP | PAN_KMOD_BO_FLAG_NO_ZERO),
       .slab_size = 64 * 1024,
       .label = "TLS pool",
       .prealloc = false,
-- 
